CONTROL name=gather-combine-choices-are-load-bearing fired=RED legs=device:8,policy_a:4,ref_bf16:4 claims=ref_bf16,policy_a,device ref_bf16.rank_accum field-moved=1263 pin-distance 1263>0; ref_bf16.cast_after field-moved=954 pin-distance 954>0; ref_bf16.expert_rotate field-moved=16368 pin-distance 16368>1; ref_bf16.acc_f32 field-moved=2048 pin-distance 1246>0; policy_a.rank_accum field-moved=1217 pin-distance 2014>2014 [policy A: movement is the ruler, not pin distance]; policy_a.cast_after field-moved=2048 pin-distance 2016>2014 [policy A: movement is the ruler, not pin distance]; policy_a.expert_rotate field-moved=16384 pin-distance 16369>16139 [policy A: movement is the ruler, not pin distance]; policy_a.acc_bf16 field-moved=2048 pin-distance 2010>2014 [policy A: movement is the ruler, not pin distance]. Every one of these is a mistake the engine could actually make and each one moves the field it claims to; on the licensed path it also has to land further from the pin than the honest arm, and on policy A that last comparison is deliberately not made — the honest arm is not licensed against those pins there, so distance to them is not a licence the mistake could fail. No limit here is invented: the comparison is against the same pins the rows are judged on, which is what licenses calling the honest arm closer
