CONTROL name=gdn-state-transposition-reddens fired=RED legs=device:1,host_cpubody:2 claims=host_cpubody,device 3 compiled legs (g++ twin, hipcc host path, and hipcc device kernels) ran `state_xpose` through `m2d_state_dot`: q_hat and k_hat bit-identical to each arm's honest record, all five state-reading stages moved, none of them closer to the pin than honest, and at least one strictly further on each arm; the arm's own reach table named exactly those five, and the transposed record comes back REJECTED on at least one of the four licensed stages (`band_reddened_on` per leg), so what reddens is the licence and not a distance this file chose. The transposition is invisible to shape checks (d_k == d_v == 128) and visible here because the pinned incoming state has 509952 live words
CONTROL name=gdn-carry-index-reddens fired=RED legs=host_cpubody:2 claims=host_cpubody both compiled arms took the decay multiplier from head (h+1) % 32: the fingerprint of the state bytes they read is UNCHANGED from the honest run (2525565901 and 3508630800 both equal the driver's own fold) while all five state-derived fields move and none gets closer to the pin, so the difference is in what the step carried and not in what it read. host_twin[same_state_read=yes input_only_identical=True state_stages_moved=True strictly_further=scan_out,core_attn,state,normed,y]; hip_hostpath[same_state_read=yes input_only_identical=True state_stages_moved=True strictly_further=scan_out,core_attn,state,normed,y]
CONTROL name=gdn-non-carried-state-reddens fired=RED legs=host_cpubody:4 claims=host_cpubody two legs, both compilers, executed: zeroing the state span in the slab leaves q_hat and k_hat bit-identical, leaves the state row very far from the pin, and moves the arm's fingerprint to exactly the all-zero fold the driver computes over those bytes; the arm's own zero-state fault reports reads_state=0 and a zero fingerprint, which the driver's reconciliation requires rather than permits. host_twin[bytes-zeroed=RED(arm_sum=0 driver_sum=0 state_ndiff 120259->417408) arm-fault=RED(reads_state=0 state_ndiff 120259->417408)]; hip_hostpath[bytes-zeroed=RED(arm_sum=0 driver_sum=0 state_ndiff 120259->417408) arm-fault=RED(reads_state=0 state_ndiff 120259->417408)]
