CONTROL name=gdn-state-read-is-the-arm-s-own-fingerprint fired=SILENT legs=device:1,host_cpubody:2 claims=host_cpubody,device reason=nothing: every honest arm's own modular fold of the state equalled the driver's fold of the same bytes on every leg this control could run on both paths, which IS the finding — the witness is not dead, because the flip legs moved it on both sides. If it ever goes quiet with fewer legs than this, the legs= count is what shows it honest legs: d_hip_device=agree(sum arm=2525565901 driver=2525565901 live=509952/509952); d_hip_hostpath=agree(sum arm=2525565901 driver=2525565901 live=509952/509952); d_host_twin=agree(sum arm=2525565901 driver=2525565901 live=509952/509952) — the arm's modular fold of the state's 524288 words equals the driver's fold of the bytes it wrote, on every arm that ran, with 509952 live words as a non-zero denominator. Flip legs: host_twin[fingerprint 2525565901->2525566144 agrees=True state_ndiff 120259->85188 scan_out_ndiff 3525->3511]; hip_hostpath[fingerprint 2525565901->2525566144 agrees=True state_ndiff 120259->85188 scan_out_ndiff 3525->3511]; hip_device[fingerprint 2525565901->2525566144 agrees=True state_ndiff 120259->120260 scan_out_ndiff 3525->3525] — flipping one byte of the state's 77,777th word moves the fingerprint on both sides, keeps them equal, and pushes the state row further from the pin while no derived row gets closer, so the number is a witness of the read and not a constant the arm prints.
CONTROL name=gdn-form-not-merged fired=RED legs=host_cpubody:2 claims=host_cpubody the arm reported form=recurrent on every one of its 3 parsed run records (recurrent); `chunked|pinned` grants 0 of the seven rows at this pass (so the two forms are not interchangeable here, which is the premise of this whole vertical); both binaries refused a plan declaring form=chunked (host_twin:form-not-implemented,hip_hostpath:form-not-implemented); 4 ACCEPTED rows all name `recurrent|pinned` in their licence and every granted stage is among them (none). Honest legs ran under both compilers so the claim is about executed reports.
CONTROL name=gdn-poison-census-can-be-nonzero fired=RED the honest record carries no poison in any of the seven fields on either compiler; forbidding one stage each makes its own field read entirely poison (host_twin[skip-carry field=state poison=524288/524288 q_hat=0 k_hat=0]; hip_hostpath[skip-out field=scan_out poison=4096/4096 q_hat=0 k_hat=0]), which is the leg that shows the census can be non-zero instead of merely printing zero
CONTROL name=gdn-plan-refusals-fire fired=RED 10 refusals across two binaries, each named: host_twin/state-is-bf16:field-elt; host_twin/v_pre-wrong-words:field-words; host_twin/missing-g_decay:field-missing; host_twin/chunked-lane-mode:mode-unknown; host_twin/gather-lane-fault:fault-unknown; hip_hostpath/state-is-bf16:field-elt; hip_hostpath/v_pre-wrong-words:field-words; hip_hostpath/missing-g_decay:field-missing; hip_hostpath/chunked-lane-mode:mode-unknown; hip_hostpath/gather-lane-fault:fault-unknown. A plan this arm should not be able to run is refused before a byte is read, which is what makes the honest run's spans worth something
