CHECK name=compiled-pair-same-census verdict=PASS the two compilers report the same read census, item census and unwritten-slot census (1 distinct tuples over 3 arms), so neither codegen silently dropped a stage before a row could hide it
CHECK name=compiled-pair-byte-identical verdict=PASS host_twin vs hip_hostpath over 22532 bytes: ndiff_bytes=0 at zero tolerance. A non-zero here is a codegen finding, never a band to absorb
CHECK name=span-digests-bind-the-arm-slab verdict=PASS 4 spans, each the same sha256 in the file, in the device read-back and in the arm's slab, so the kernel reads bytes the staging path certified
CHECK name=no-accepted-row-without-a-licence verdict=PASS accepted=9 unlicensed_accepts=0
CHECK name=every-unlicensed-row-names-stage-and-reason verdict=PASS unlicensed=8 malformed=0 — the residue is reported, never dissolved
CHECK name=pass-unreachable-while-rows-unlicensed verdict=PASS unlicensed=8; PASS would require zero
CHECK name=band-digest-pinned verdict=PASS band_digest=27a68c7e82c9aa05 pinned=27a68c7e82c9aa05
CHECK name=device-claims-come-from-device-only verdict=PASS device ran=True counted hip calls=16(python)+448(arm); device-shaped lines=3 ['BLOCKDEVICE', 'PROVENANCE', 'PROVENANCE'] — the claim and the witness must appear together or not at all
CHECK name=hip-witness-matches-mode verdict=PASS staged_runs=4 launches=146 allocs=112 bytes_to_device=839032304 bytes_from_device=20357384 in a device run
CHECK name=arm-reports-parsed-completely verdict=PASS 3 arm runs, each parsed into HDR/PLAN/RUN/WROTE/RESULT; a report that parses nothing cannot fail
CHECK name=no-rate-figures-in-output verdict=PASS scanned 436 printed lines against the rate-token list and found none; the list is not printed here because the scan covers this line too
CHECK name=pinned-digests-verified-on-every-dump-read verdict=PASS files_read=278 bytes_read=92604352 (every dump read sha256-checked against its manifest record)
CHECK name=rt-arm-stages-equal-manifest-population verdict=PASS this path declares router_logits,topk_ids,topk_weights; the licensor's own router family is router_logits,topk_ids,topk_weights — the must-produce set and the licence set are read from the same tuple, so they cannot drift
CHECK name=rt-geometry-matches-the-config verdict=PASS MR_E=256 cfg n_experts=256, MR_H=2048 cfg d=2048, MR_K=8 cfg top_k=8: the prototype header's router geometry and the checkpoint's must be the same numbers before a row means anything
CHECK name=rt-census-equals-geometry verdict=PASS element reads and item counts required to equal the geometry (E*H of weight, E*H of activation re-read per expert, 256 logit items and 1 serial item): bad=none; rt_hip_device[reads_w=524288 reads_x=524288 items=256/1 path=device]; rt_hip_hostpath[reads_w=524288 reads_x=524288 items=256/1 path=host_cpubody]; rt_host_twin[reads_w=524288 reads_x=524288 items=256/1 path=host_cpubody]
CHECK name=rt-compiled-pair-byte-identical verdict=PASS g++ twin vs hipcc host path over the router record, one source, -ffp-contract=off on both: host_twin_vs_hip_hostpath bytes=22532 ndiff_bytes=0 device=False; rt_host_twin_vs_rt_hip_hostpath bytes=3232 ndiff_bytes=0 device=False; rt_hip_device_vs_rt_hip_hostpath bytes=0 ndiff_bytes=0 device=True. Zero tolerance, because `topk_weights` is licensed at exactness and a compiler that disagreed about the renormalisation is exactly the finding that must not be absorbed into a band; the zero-tolerance pair is host-vs-host by construction, and a device leg (present only with --device, marked device=False,False,True below) is compared to the host leg on the claimed fields alone, under `rt-device-host-claimed-fields-identical`, because `prototype/moe_router/moe_router_kernels.h` §mr_exp documents that the two libms' exp() may differ by an ULP
CHECK name=rt-ids-are-a-selection verdict=PASS the honest record's 8 ids are in range, distinct, and the two tie rules selected the same 8 experts in some order (this row has no exact tie at the boundary, so the rules coincide here — `topk-selection-perturbations-redden-ids` is what shows they need not)
CHECK name=rt-poison-census-zero-on-the-honest-record verdict=PASS all 8 fields of the honest router record are fully written: ids=0,ids_alt=0,logits=0,logits_f32=0,probs=0,wcast=0,wleak=0,wpre=0. The non-zero leg is controlled separately, and a census that could only read 0 would prove nothing either way
CHECK name=rt-ulp-ruler-matches-the-licensor verdict=PASS `wpre` measured twice, once by `engine/block_gate.py`::ulp_diff (the licensor's ruler, aggregate only) and once per slot by `rt_ulp_slots` here: licensor ndiff=5 max_ulp=2, here ndiff=5 max_ulp=2 over 8 slots. The two folds are the same map widened to int64, and if they ever disagree the ULP number in this file means something different from the ULP number in every band
CHECK name=rt-wpre-scope-derived-from-artifacts verdict=PASS the scope on `wpre` (9 ULP on pair `rt_hip_device_vs_rt_hip_hostpath`) is the strictest of three priors — a licensor floor probe, §R5's wording, and an error propagation from §mr_exp's — and none of them is this build's output. The dependence on the licensor's artifact is witnessed, not claimed: the triangle prior is exactly twice `weights_vs_pinned_f32_ulp` as the artifact reads it (5 x 2 = 10), and re-deriving with that number set to 1 in memory makes the prior 2 (the binding limit would then be 2). A bound typed into this file would not move. Wording the driver cannot find in its source documents is a refusal, not a default
CHECK name=rt-wpre-premise-measured-against-the-pin verdict=PASS the triangle-inequality prior only holds if both compilations are themselves inside the licensed band of the pinned pre-cast weights: device=4,host_twin=2 ULP against a licensed `weights_vs_pinned_f32_ulp` of 5. If a route drifts past its own licence the premise fails and this reddens, rather than letting a bound derived from two licensed legs license a third number nobody licensed
CHECK name=rt-device-launch-counted verdict=PASS the device arm counted at least one launch and one HIP call; the flag is not the evidence, the counter is
CHECK name=rt-device-host-licensed-fields-identical verdict=PASS device arm vs host twin, zero tolerance on the fields a licence measures at exactness: ids=0/8,ids_alt=0/8,wcast=0/8 (whole record ndiff_bytes=237 of 3232, which is not this claim — the rest of those bytes are the `wpre` scope and the long-dot `probs`, both printed and neither absorbed). The tolerance-free form is the point: one differing bit of `topk_ids` or of the bf16 `topk_weights` reddens this check and cannot hide inside `wpre`'s measured spread, because those rows are licensed at exactness by `speccheck/spec.md §10.6` and the licensor's floor probe measured 164 f32 ULP of margin against a 5 ULP route spread before it agreed the cast was robust
CHECK name=rt-device-host-wpre-within-derived-scope verdict=PASS `wpre` (the fp32 pre-cast renormalised weight) between the two compilations: 5 of 8 slots differ, worst 2 ULP, per-slot 1,1,1,0,0,0,2,1, against the derived scope of 9 ULP in `WPRESCOPE`. This is a re-derivation, not a relaxation: §R5 documents the field as not bit-exact across an independent fp32 route, the limit comes from that document, §mr_exp's, and the licensor's floor probe, and `CONTROL name=wpre-scope-rejects-a-bigger-perturbation` witnesses that the limit rejects a larger-than-scope perturbation. Measuring the spread and enforcing what came out would be a gate that reddens on nothing
CHECK name=rt-device-host-difference-is-the-documented-exp-scope verdict=PASS attribution, because 'the two libms differ' is a story until each named condition is separately answerable: R1's outputs bit-identical=True, `wcast` bit-identical=True, every moving `wpre` slot has its own `probs` addend moving=True, fields moving outside the exp() path=none. All four hold, so the difference is the documented `exp()` scope and the fix belongs in the check. If any had failed it would be a codegen defect and the fix would belong in `engine/device/m2_rt_kernels.h`, which is why this is a check and not a sentence in a log
CHECK name=control-legs-cover-the-path-under-claim verdict=PASS 13 of 29 controls declare which path they covered, and every declared path has at least one arm act counted off that arm's own `RUN path=` report: gather-census-proves-slices-not-whole-tensor=ref_bf16:1,policy_a:1,device:2; gather-combine-choices-are-load-bearing=ref_bf16:4,policy_a:4,device:8; gather-device-unit-read-back=device:2; gather-divergence-causes-priced=host_cpubody:25; gather-gate-up-swap-reddens=ref_bf16:2,policy_a:1,device:3; gather-poison-census-nonzero-and-attributed=ref_bf16:3,policy_a:3,device:6; gdn-carry-index-reddens=host_cpubody:2; gdn-form-not-merged=host_cpubody:2; gdn-non-carried-state-reddens=host_cpubody:4; gdn-state-read-is-the-arm-s-own-fingerprint=host_cpubody:2,device:1; gdn-state-transposition-reddens=host_cpubody:2,device:1; topk-selection-perturbations-redden-ids=host_cpubody:2,device:2; wpre-scope-rejects-a-bigger-perturbation=host_cpubody:1,device:1. Controls declaring no path (their legs are plan/refusal legs, not path legs): control-witness-guard-can-redden,device-claim-scan-is-awake,gather-device-ask-refuses-instead-of-substituting,gather-read-back-expectation-is-the-artifact,gather-width-substitution-refused,gdn-device-ask-refuses-instead-of-substituting,gdn-divergence-causes-priced,gdn-plan-refusals-fire,gdn-poison-census-can-be-nonzero,launch-failure-exits-red,poison-census-can-be-nonzero,resident-span-corrupt,router-dtype-order-distinguishable-in-arm,router-poison-census-can-be-nonzero,router-span-is-f32,wrong-modes-further-from-pins. Window e2 is the reason this check exists: `topk-selection-perturbations-redden-ids` claimed the device path while both its legs ran on the host twin, and read SILENT in the mode everything above M2 is built on
CHECK name=device-path-claims-executed-on-device verdict=PASS a device run has to have run the perturbation controls on the device, not merely beside it: 26 control legs executed under `path=device` (the licensed-row controls need their tie and bound legs on the arm they license). In a CPU run this check is vacuous by construction and says so, because there is no device path to claim
CHECK name=silent-control-names-its-reason verdict=PASS every control that did not fire also printed a `reason=` naming what it could not do: 26 of 29 controls fired, and the ones that went quiet are none. Window `g` is why this is a check and not a style rule: `control-witness-guard-can-redden` printed a quiet line with no reason on the device path, which reads exactly like a guard that ran and found nothing. A control that cannot run a leg prints that leg as not-exercised instead; a control that goes quiet names the finding
CHECK name=field-attribution-accounts-to-the-pair verdict=PASS 35 per-field attribution tables were printed (paired totals: g_ref_bf16_host_twin_vs_hip_hostpath=0/0;g_ref_bf16_hip_device_vs_hip_hostpath=0/0;g_policy_a_host_twin_vs_hip_hostpath=0/0;g_policy_a_hip_device_vs_hip_hostpath=3744/3744;d_host_twin_vs_d_hip_hostpath=0/0;d_host_twin_vs_d_hip_hostpath=0/0) and in every one the field counts add up to the ndiff_bytes of the pair they belong to. A per-field table that did not account would be measuring a different population than the PAIR line it explains, and a run that printed no attribution at all would satisfy this check trivially, which is why the count is required non-zero here rather than assumed
CHECK name=gather-rows-equal-licensed-stages verdict=PASS rows=4 expected=4: expert_raw,routed_sum on each of ref_bf16,policy_a. Both stages exist on both width paths by design: one is what a band can license, the other is what the engine ships
CHECK name=gather-policy-a-rows-unlicensed-by-name verdict=PASS the policy-A pair prints UNLICENSED with reason `policy-a-width-band-absent`, and nothing above counts them as accepted: no band measures a quantized arm against bf16 pins, and the floor probe that would license it has never been run
CHECK name=gather-licence-names-its-source verdict=PASS the licensed rows print where the limit came from: expert_raw:floor-probe(legitimate_reassociation_layer0),routed_sum:spec-10.6(exactness) — a number with no licensor is not a band
CHECK name=gather-census-agrees-with-the-plan verdict=PASS per expert_index, driver-vs-arm agreement over all 2 paths, with a non-zero denominator on both sides and no note conflict: policy_a units=24/24 spans=24/24 bytes=15204352 whole=0 conflict=0; ref_bf16 units=24/24 spans=16/16 bytes=50331648 whole=0 conflict=0. A whole-tensor read would move distinct_experts, bytes per expert, or both, and prediction 2's scheduler decision is made on those numbers; a census that counted nothing, or an arm whose census note was overwritten, would satisfy the agreement trivially and so is refused here rather than allowed to pass 
CHECK name=gather-distinct-experts-equals-top-k verdict=PASS every path touched exactly K=8 distinct expert indices for K slots: a gather that walked the whole expert axis would report 256 here instead, and an empty census would report nothing at all, which is refused rather than skipped
CHECK name=gather-honest-record-has-no-unwritten-slot verdict=PASS the honest records carry no NaN in any field on either path (offending: none); the poison control is what shows that count can be non-zero
CHECK name=gather-compiled-pair-byte-identical-per-path verdict=FAIL per width path, g++ twin vs hipcc: policy_a bytes=122880 ndiff=3744,ref_bf16 bytes=122880 ndiff=0 at zero tolerance. One aggregate would let one path cancel the other's difference
CHECK name=gather-read-set-forms-come-from-the-file verdict=PASS the policy-A gather reads 24 expert units and every unit's arm `kind`, block count and byte count are derived from the tensor's own ggml type in the artifact header (GFORMAT lines), with each declared byte count equal to blocks x block-bytes-of-that-kind. The same table prints the declared policy-A type beside the stored one because D-27's fact — expert down_proj stored at Q5_K/Q6_K where policy A declares Q4_K, admitted by loader.py's floor rule with no waiver — is why a width hypothesis had to be priced and not dismissed: 8 of 24 units are wider-than-declared. offences: none
CHECK name=gather-unlicensed-counted-not-absorbed verdict=PASS the gather tally carries licensed=2 accepted=2 rejected=0 unlicensed=2; the policy-A rows are counted as unlicensed rather than dropped, and PASS remains unreachable while any row is unlicensed
CHECK name=gather-device-path-claims-executed-on-device verdict=PASS in a device run every gather device arm reported launches>0 (2 device arms); in a CPU window the same --device ask on the g++ twin is refused with a named tag instead of a host run, and this check is vacuous here and says so
CHECK name=gather-control-legs-cover-the-width-under-claim verdict=PASS 4 gather controls declared width paths, each with the legs it claims: gather-census-proves-slices-not-whole-tensor[ref_bf16:1,policy_a:1]; gather-combine-choices-are-load-bearing[ref_bf16:4,policy_a:4]; gather-gate-up-swap-reddens[ref_bf16:2,policy_a:1]; gather-poison-census-nonzero-and-attributed[ref_bf16:3,policy_a:3]. Controls whose only leg is a named refusal, which declares no path because no arm ran to completion: gather-device-ask-refuses-instead-of-substituting,gather-device-unit-read-back,gather-divergence-causes-priced,gather-read-back-expectation-is-the-artifact,gather-width-substitution-refused. The width tally is counted by `g_arm` off the plan the run used, the same way window e2's lesson made the host/device claim cost something. Failures, if any: none
CHECK name=gdn-rows-equal-licensor-stage-list verdict=PASS 7 rows, one per stage the licensor's `SCAN_WIDTH_STAGES` and the layer-0 GDN manifest agree on; the arm's record field names are the same set (q_hat,k_hat,scan_out,core_attn,state,normed,y missing=none extra=none), so a rename on either side reddens instead of dropping a row
CHECK name=gdn-kernel-geometry-matches-the-config verdict=PASS the prototype header's GDN_H=2048 GDN_H_K=16 GDN_H_V=32 GDN_D_K=128 GDN_D_V=128 GDN_EXP=2 against the checkpoint config's d=2048 h_k=16 h_v=32 d_k=128 d_v=128 expansion=2: every record offset and every item count in the arm is an expression over the header's constants, so the two rulers have to be shown to read the same model
CHECK name=gdn-arm-implements-only-the-form-it-claims verdict=PASS the arm's declared form is `recurrent` on every run (recurrent), which is the pair `block_gate.adjudicate` credits GDN rows under and the only value `engine/device/m2_d_io.h` accepts in a plan; the row credit and the form claim are checked against each other in CONTROL gdn-form-not-merged
CHECK name=gdn-census-equals-geometry-and-driver verdict=PASS per arm, the arm's own item, read, write and output counts equal what the geometry implies AND its fingerprint of the state equals the driver's fold of the bytes it supplied, with a non-zero live-word denominator on both sides: d_hip_device[state=2525565901/2525565901 disagree=none]; d_hip_hostpath[state=2525565901/2525565901 disagree=none]; d_host_twin[state=2525565901/2525565901 disagree=none]. The reconciliation is what turns a census from a decoration into a claim — an arm that skipped the carry, read the state transposed in a way that missed words, or read a stale slab disagrees here rather than printing a tidy 0
CHECK name=gdn-honest-record-has-no-unwritten-slot verdict=PASS the honest record carries no poison in any of its seven fields (offending fields: none); the poison control is the leg that shows that count can be non-zero
CHECK name=gdn-compiled-pair-byte-identical verdict=FAIL g++ twin vs hipcc host path over 2187264 B: ndiff_bytes=0 at zero tolerance, and device vs host path ndiff_bytes=52976. A non-zero here is a codegen finding, never a band to absorb: the two compilers are handed one arithmetic (`engine/device/m2_d_kernels.h` is the only place it is written), so agreement is what the shared body promises and disagreement is a compiler question, not a licence question
CHECK name=gdn-state-span-binds-the-arm-slab verdict=PASS 9 spans, each the same sha256 in the dump file and in the arm's slab, so the kernel reads bytes the dump reader certified (q_pre=b7af6307,k_pre=a1b0909a,v_pre=ebc42dcb,beta=fece6f6a,g_decay=79a8d63b,z=78ae71eb,norm_w=7ebc1757,out_w=cc08048a,state_in=214d4694)
CHECK name=gdn-cross-implementation-comparison-was-made verdict=PASS the arm was compared to the engine's own torch GDN body over all 7 stages (q_hat=1178/4096,k_hat=820/4096,scan_out=3525/4096,core_attn=0/4096,state=120259/524288,normed=0/4096,y=1/2048), and that body's own distance to the pins was measured over the same comparator (q_hat=0/4096,k_hat=0/4096,scan_out=0/4096,core_attn=0/4096,state=0/524288,normed=0/4096,y=0/2048) so the two numbers cannot be read as two wrong programs agreeing. Neither line is a licensor — the rows are judged against the pinned records by `block_gate.adjudicate`, and a difference from the torch body is reported and investigated, never absorbed. Three spellings of §04b.1 (g++, hipcc, torch) is the answer to 'is this just one arm compared to itself'
CHECK name=gdn-licensed-rows-name-the-arm-form-and-no-others verdict=PASS 4 of 7 GDN rows are ACCEPTED and each names `recurrent|pinned` in its licence, which is the pair the arm's own form word claims; the remaining 3 print the licensor's own reason, counted not dissolved (core_attn:arm-pair-not-licensed-at-pass,normed:arm-pair-not-licensed-at-pass,y:arm-pair-not-licensed-at-pass). The grant set was re-derived by asking band_licenses per stage, so this check does not take the row list's word for what it licensed
CHECK name=gdn-unlicensed-counted-not-absorbed verdict=PASS the GDN tally carries licensed=4 accepted=4 rejected=0 unlicensed=3; PASS stays unreachable while a GDN row is unlicensed, which includes the 3 rows no form's band covers at this pass
